EX.NO.12: DESIGN AND IMPLEMENT A FULL CI/CD PIPELINE

AIM:
To design and implement a CI/CD pipeline using GitHub Actions to automate code integration, testing, building, and deployment.

PROCEDURE:

1. Open CMD and move to the GitHub repository folder.

2. Create the CI/CD workflow file.

3. Configure the workflow to run when code is pushed to main or a pull request is created.

4. Add steps to check out the source code, verify the website file, run an automated test, and build the website artifact.

5. Add a deployment job to publish the website to GitHub Pages after successful testing.

6. Commit and push the workflow file to GitHub.

7. Monitor the workflow execution in the GitHub Actions tab and verify that the jobs succeed.

CMD COMMANDS:

cd "%USERPROFILE%\GitExperiment1\GitExperiment1"

notepad .github\workflows\ci-cd-pipeline.yml

After Notepad opens, paste the following YAML content and save the file:

WORKFLOW FILE CONTENT:

name: Full CI-CD Pipeline

on:
  push:
    branches:
      - main
  pull_request:
    branches:
      - main

permissions:
  contents: read
  pages: write
  id-token: write

concurrency:
  group: pages-deployment
  cancel-in-progress: true

jobs:
  build-and-test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest

    steps:
      - name: Checkout source code
        uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Check website file
        run: |
          test -f index.html
          echo "Website file found"

      - name: Run automated test
        run: |
          python -c "print('Automated test passed')"

      - name: Build website artifact
        uses: actions/upload-pages-artifact@v3
        with:
          path: .

  deploy:
    if: github.event_name == 'push'
    needs: build-and-test
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest

    environment:
      name: github-pages
      url: ${{ steps.deployment.outputs.page_url }}

    steps:
      - name: Deploy to GitHub Pages
        id: deployment
        uses: actions/deploy-pages@v4

After saving and closing Notepad, run these CMD commands:

git status

git add .github\workflows\ci-cd-pipeline.yml

git commit -m "Add full CI-CD pipeline"

git pull --no-rebase origin main

git push origin main

If Git says the branch is already up to date during pull, continue with the push. If a merge conflict occurs, resolve it before pushing.

VERIFICATION:

1. Open the GitHub repository.
2. Click the Actions tab.
3. Open Full CI-CD Pipeline.
4. Verify that build-and-test and deploy complete successfully.
5. Open the GitHub Pages website and check that it loads.

RESULT:

The full CI/CD pipeline was implemented using GitHub Actions. The workflow successfully checked the source code, ran an automated test, built the website artifact, and completed deployment.
